{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"694c391740c88ca14657e9ea3ebe630027570b9054985aeb9e17a5e35544a972","digest":{"component_or_area":"fallback-endpoint test","key_entities":["tests/unit/test_llm_fallback_chain.py","test_a_fallback_entry_endpoint_is_built_against_that_endpoint","model.models[1].base_url","model.models[0].base_url","_origin","urllib.parse.urlsplit","_FALLBACK_ENDPOINT","py/incomplete-url-substring-sanitization"],"problem_keywords":["incomplete url substring sanitization","weak assertion","url origin comparison","codeql alert"],"propositions":["Two CodeQL high-severity alerts flag URL prefix checks (startswith) in fallback-endpoint assertions that accept hosts merely sharing the endpoint prefix as a substring.","The assertions check by startswith instead of comparing parsed URL origins, allowing a prefix-sharing look-alike host (e.g. https://fallback.test.evil.example) to satisfy the test incorrectly.","The fix replaces startswith substring tests with exact equality comparison of parsed URL origins (scheme, netloc tuple) via urllib.parse.urlsplit, eliminating both the CodeQL alert and the weak assertion.","The test property — that the fallback entry is built against the configured endpoint rather than the provider default — is preserved and verified through mutation testing."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787492734517232001,"uuid":"64afe3f2-a308-4f63-ade8-16af80f90970"}